 To see that the set theoretic condition of that lemma is satisfied we argue as follows: First choose the open covering such that $|I| \leq \text{size}(V)$. Next, choose schemes $U_ i$ of size $\leq \max (\kappa , \text{size}(V))$ and surjective étale morphisms $U_ i \to Z_ i$; we can do this by assumption (2) and Sets, Lemma <a href="/tag/04T6" data-tag="04T6">3.9.6</a> (details omitted). Then Sets, Lemma <a href="/tag/000R" data-tag="000R">3.9.9</a> implies that $\coprod U_ i$ is an object of $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. Hence $\coprod Z_ i$ is an algebraic space by Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/02WQ" data-tag="02WQ">65.8.4</a>. 